# Claude Code — ignore contents (`.claude/*`, not `.claude/`: git never
# descends into a fully-excluded dir, which made the re-include dead) but
# track the session commands.
.claude/*
!.claude/commands/
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/settings.json

# Lab autonomous-R&D scratch output — the overnight loop commits per-cycle data
# dumps (data/, data_after/, data_test/). ~2,587 files / ~7.7MB already tracked;
# this stops NEW cycles from adding more. To untrack the existing ones (working
# tree preserved, no history rewrite):
#   git rm -r --cached lab/experiments
# See docs/BACKLOG.md item H1.
lab/experiments/*/data/
lab/experiments/*/data_after/
lab/experiments/*/data_test/
lab/experiments/**/*.json

# Raw session transcript committed by mistake (space in filename, no extension).
# Untrack with: git rm --cached "docs/v2 session transcript"
docs/v2 session transcript

# Coverage artifacts
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Machine-specific MCP wiring (absolute paths)
.mcp.json
engine/data/

# Opportunity-funnel runtime cache (symbol list, regenerated on a 7d TTL).
# The RUN OUTPUT (docs/opportunity_funnel_run.json) is committed; this is not.
backend/data/funnel_cache/

# LLM-SWARM-1 session logs. The ARTIFACTS (frozen universe, per-cell
# checkpoint, run metadata) are committed beside them; the raw stdout of a run
# is not an artifact, and yfinance's per-ticker noise is not evidence.
backend/data/swarm/*.log

# WRDS bulk-pull operational state. These are rewritten every few tables
# while a multi-hour pull runs, and they are TRACKED, so a running pull
# made `git status` dirty continuously — which on 2026-08-20 flipped the
# 17:00 launcher receipt's `git_dirty` from False to True and would have
# contaminated the arming pre-flight. A day session's data churn must
# never be able to do that.
# The evidential content (what was pulled, what was skipped and why) is
# preserved by committing a STABLE snapshot when a pull completes, which
# is better practice than committing a file mid-rewrite.
backend/data/optimus/wrds/pull_everything_manifest.json
backend/data/optimus/wrds/pull_everything_plan.json
# Same rule for the catch-up pass (wrds_pull_catchup): a multi-hour run that
# appends a progress log must not be able to flip git_dirty at 17:00 either.
backend/data/optimus/wrds/pull_catchup_log.jsonl
backend/data/optimus/wrds/pull_terminal_failures.json

# ARENA (ORDER 25): local ledger writes must never dirty the tree the night
# launcher's git_dirty check reads. Railway's volume is the authoritative store.
backend/data/optimus/arena/
# Runtime receipts written by pi_hourly_mtm on the prod volume; local test
# runs of the scheduler job write real ones here too. Runtime state, not source.
backend/data/optimus/mtm_receipts/
# Generic scheduled-job receipts (services/job_receipts.py). Runtime
# evidence, per-deploy, pruned per job — not source.
backend/data/optimus/job_receipts/
backend/data/optimus/wrds/truncated_quarantine.json
backend/data/optimus/wrds/substrate_verification.json
backend/data/optimus/prediction_markets/
backend/data/optimus/aegis_panel/screen_cache/
# panel-2 planted-world run artifacts: per-(world, arm, fold) IC cache and run
# logs. Regenerable from the panel, and the RECEIPTS (panel2_detectability/)
# are the committed output — the cache is scaffolding, not evidence.
backend/data/optimus/aegis_panel/panel2_planted_cache/
backend/data/optimus/aegis_panel/panel2_planted.log
backend/data/optimus/aegis_panel/panel2_planted.err
backend/data/optimus/aegis_panel/panel2_planted.done

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bulk WRDS pulls that exceed the 20MB "commit the receipt, not the raw data"
# line (added 2026-09-03). These are RAW SUBSTRATE, regenerable from WRDS by
# their own pull scripts; the derived RECEIPTS in
# backend/data/optimus/tracker_backtest/ are the committed evidence.
# Every ignored artefact is catalogued in docs/DATA_MANIFEST.md with its size,
# its producer and how to rebuild it -- an untracked file that is not in the
# manifest is a file nobody can find again.
backend/data/optimus/wrds/crsp_monthly_panel_2013_2024.json
backend/data/optimus/wrds/tr13f_quarterly.json

# Key backups. `.env.hidden` above covers the CI-mimic recipe; this covers the
# dated hand-made backups. They contain LIVE keys. Never staged, never moved
# by a session -- if one needs to leave the tree, a human moves it.
.env.bak
.env.bak.*

# learner/states: the sweep cache that `--reuse-assignments` reads. Derived
# from the parquets above and duplicated inside the receipt.
backend/data/optimus/learner/states/sweep_meta*.json

# EDGAR 8-K item-code TAPE (87 MB, 293,619 rows). A DERIVED tape, rebuilt by
# `scripts/edgar_8k_items.py` from filings we already have; the RECEIPT beside
# it is committed. GitHub warns above 50 MB and rejects above 100 MB, and this
# repo is public. Data manifest: docs/DATA_MANIFEST.md.
backend/data/optimus/edgar_8k/*.jsonl
